{
  "id": "2CH.30",
  "number": "30",
  "bookId": "2CH",
  "reference": "2 Chronicles 30",
  "verseCount": 25,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "30",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "2CH 30"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "30",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.1+2CH.30.2+2CH.30.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.1",
              "2CH.30.2",
              "2CH.30.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "NUM.9.9+NUM.9.10+NUM.9.11"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Num 9.9–11",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The people had not been able to celebrate the Passover Festival at the proper time, in the first month, because not enough priests were ritually clean and not many people had assembled in Jerusalem. So King Hezekiah, his officials, and the people of Jerusalem agreed to celebrate it in the second month, and the king sent word to all the people of Israel and Judah. He took special care to send letters to the tribes of Ephraim and Manasseh, inviting them to come to the Temple in Jerusalem to celebrate the Passover in honour of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.1+2CH.30.2+2CH.30.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.1",
              "2CH.30.2",
              "2CH.30.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.1+2CH.30.2+2CH.30.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.1",
              "2CH.30.2",
              "2CH.30.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The king and the people were pleased with their plan, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "so they invited all the Israelites, from Dan in the north to Beersheba in the south, to come together in Jerusalem and celebrate the Passover according to the Law, in larger numbers than ever before. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Messengers went out at the command of the king and his officials through all Judah and Israel with the following invitation:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“People of Israel, you have survived the Assyrian conquest of the land. Now return to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and he will return to you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not be like your ancestors and your fellow-Israelites who were unfaithful to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " their God. As you can see, he punished them severely. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not be stubborn as they were, but obey the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". Come to the Temple in Jerusalem, which the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God has made holy for ever, and worship him so that he will no longer be angry with you. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If you return to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", then those who have taken your relatives away as prisoners will take pity on them and let them come back home. The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " your God is kind and merciful, and if you return to him, he will accept you.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The messengers went to every city in the territory of the tribes of Ephraim and Manasseh, and as far north as the tribe of Zebulun, but people laughed at them and ridiculed them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Still, there were some from the tribes of Asher, Manasseh, and Zebulun who were willing to come to Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "God was also at work in Judah and united the people in their determination to obey his will by following the commands of the king and his officials.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A great number of people gathered in Jerusalem in the second month to celebrate the Festival of Unleavened Bread. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They took all the altars that had been used in Jerusalem for offering sacrifices and burning incense and threw them into the valley of the Kidron. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And on the fourteenth day of the month they killed the lambs for the Passover sacrifice. The priests and Levites who were not ritually clean were so ashamed that they dedicated themselves to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", and now they could sacrifice burnt offerings in the Temple. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They took their places in the Temple according to the instructions in the Law of Moses, the man of God. The Levites gave the blood of the sacrifices to the priests, who sprinkled it on the altar. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because many of the people were not ritually clean, they could not kill the Passover lambs, so the Levites did it for them, and dedicated the lambs to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In addition, many of those who had come from the tribes of Ephraim, Manasseh, Issachar, and Zebulun had not performed the ritual of purification, and so they were observing Passover improperly. King Hezekiah offered this prayer for them: ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“O ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of our ancestors, in your goodness forgive those who are worshipping you with all their heart, even though they are not ritually clean.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " answered Hezekiah's prayer; he forgave the people and did not harm them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For seven days the people who had gathered in Jerusalem celebrated the Festival of Unleavened Bread with great joy, and day after day the Levites and the priests praised the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " with all their strength.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30.21",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Probable text",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "with all their strength",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "with mighty instruments.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hezekiah praised the Levites for their skill in conducting the worship of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.22"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "After the seven days during which they offered sacrifices in praise of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of their ancestors, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "they all decided to celebrate for another seven days. So they celebrated with joy. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "King Hezekiah contributed 1,000 bulls and 7,000 sheep for the people to kill and eat, and the officials gave them another thousand bulls and 10,000 sheep. A large number of priests went through the ritual of purification. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So everyone was happy — the people of Judah, the priests, the Levites, the people who had come from the north, and the foreigners who had settled permanently in Israel and Judah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2CH 30:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The city of Jerusalem was filled with joy, because nothing like this had happened since the days of King Solomon, the son of David. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2CH.30.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2CH.30.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
